<p>Last year, Apple <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2025/09/apple-adds-iphones-to-friday-night-baseball-coverage/">integrated the iPhone 17 Pro</a> into its Friday Night Baseball coverage. As you might expect, this year it’s doing the same with the recently announced iPhone 18 Pro.</p>
<p>According to Apple, <a href="https://tv.apple.com/us/room/edt.item.62327df1-6874-470e-98b2-a5bbeac509a2">its coverage of Friday’s Giants-Dodgers game at Dodger Stadium</a> will include 14 different iPhone 18 Pros “embedded throughout Dodger Stadium,” including in the pitch clock, backstop, foul pole, and both bullpens. The idea is to provide unusual vantage points that haven’t been seen in baseball broadcasts before.</p>
<p>In addition, Friday’s game marks the fourth <a href="https://sixcolors.com/post/2026/08/apple-takes-first-immersive-baseball-swings-from-the-on-deck-circle/">immersive broadcast</a> of the season, providing a you-are-there perspective for Vision Pro users.</p>
<p>This is the last Friday Night Baseball game of this year.</p>
